          "text": "{\"regions\":{\"r2\":{\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"lines\":[{\"n\":1,\"text\":\"&c.-To be brief, in short. \u0935\u091f\u0935\u093f\u091f\u092a\u0903 &c-it is difficult to see the\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":2,\"text\":\"propriety of calling the Vata tree \u2018a dayita\u2019; probably the poet\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":3,\"text\":\"refers by dayita\u2019 to \u0917\u0943\u0939\u0938\u094d\u0925\u093e\u0936\u094d\u0930\u092e in which the wife plays a con-\",\"end\":\"hyphen\"},{\"n\":4,\"text\":\"spicuous part. Let the Vata tree be my home i. e. let me\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":5,\"text\":\"renounce the pleasures of the world and take to a devotee\u2019s life\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":6,\"text\":\"worshipping S'iva sitting under a Vata tree &c.\",\"end\":\"space\"}],\"uncertain\":true,\"note\":\"The Sanskrit quotation is somewhat unclear.\"},\"r3\":{\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"lines\":[{\"n\":1,\"text\":\"Sl. 6. \u0924\u094d\u0930\u0941\u091f\u093f\u0924 &c.\u2014the worldly ties which proved an obstruc-\",\"end\":\"hyphen\"},{\"n\":2,\"text\":\"tion to them having been snapped. \u0906\u0936\u0940\u0935\u093f\u0937\u2014a serpent; fr.\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":3,\"text\":\"\u0906\u0936\u0940 ( a serpent\u2019s fang ) + \u0935\u093f\u0937. The derivation more usually\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":4,\"text\":\"given is fr. \u0906\u0936\u0940\u0938\u094d+\u0935\u093f\u0937 the comp. being classed under the\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":5,\"text\":\"\u092a\u0943\u0937\u094b\u0926\u0930\u093e\u0926\u093f class. The 2nd l. means ( those blessed persons ) that\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":6,\"text\":\"do not seek the crooked course of serpentine sensualism. Mr.\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":7,\"text\":\"Telang takes \u0935\u093f\u0937\u092e with \u0906\u0936\u0940\u0935\u093f\u0937 and says \u2018the course of\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":8,\"text\":\"worldly objects which are like dangerous snakes.\u2019 \u0936\u0930\u091a\u094d\u091a\u0928\u094d\u0926\u094d\u0930 &c,\u2014\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":9,\"text\":\"the night which is delightful on account of the sky being lit\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":10,\"text\":\"up with the winter moonshine. \u0906\u092d\u094b\u0917\u2014expanse. ( \u091c\u094d\u092f\u094b\u0924\u093f\u0930\u0938\u094d\u092f\u0938\u094d\u092f\u093e\u0903\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":11,\"text\":\"\u0909\u0926\u094d\u092f\u094b\u0924\u0903 ). \u091a\u092f storing up. \u0936\u0930\u0923\u2014from \u0936\u0943 9 con. to tear.\",\"end\":\"space\"}],\"uncertain\":true,\"note\":\"Several Sanskrit quotations, especially at the end, are difficult to read.\"},\"r4\":{\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"lines\":[{\"n\":1,\"text\":\"Sl. 7. A question to an estranged friend. Once our in-\",\"end\":\"hyphen\"},{\"n\":2,\"text\":\"terests were identical; now you and we have no connection.\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":3,\"text\":\"What has happened in the meanwhile to estrange us ?\",\"end\":\"space\"}],\"uncertain\":false,\"note\":null},\"r5\":{\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"lines\":[{\"n\":1,\"text\":\"Sl. 8. \u0905\u092e\u0932\u092a\u091f\u0902\u2014of clean texture. \u092a\u091f\u094d\u091f\u0935\u0938\u094d\u0924\u094d\u0930\u0902\u2014silken cloth.\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":2,\"text\":\"\u0915\u0926\u0936\u0928\u0902\u2014By P\u00e1n. VI. 3. 101. ( see com. ) \u0915\u0926\u094d is substituted for\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":3,\"text\":\"\u0915\u0941 in a Tat. when the latter member begins with a vowel; coarse\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":4,\"text\":\"food. \u0935\u094d\u092f\u0915\u094d\u0924 &c.\u2014The idea is\u2014A man who has renounced the\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":5,\"text\":\"world and devoted himself to the service of God entirely is\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":6,\"text\":\"indifferent to all such things as are mentioned in the s'loka.\",\"end\":\"space\"}],\"uncertain\":true,\"note\":\"Some Sanskrit words are indistinct.\"},\"r6\":{\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"lines\":[{\"n\":1,\"text\":\"Sl. 9. \u0938\u094d\u092e\u0930 &c.\u2014Love is often described as blinding men\u2019s\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":2,\"text\":\"eyes, \u092a\u091f\u0941\u0924\u0930 &c.\u2014\u0935\u093f\u0935\u0947\u0915 is here called collyrium because it\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":3,\"text\":\"sharpens, restores, or preserves the sight of the mind. \u0938\u092e\u0940-\",\"end\":\"hyphen\"},{\"n\":4,\"text\":\"\u092d\u0942\u0924\u093e\u2014Made even, rectified, corrected. R\u00e2marshi explains it by\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":5,\"text\":\"\u0928\u093f\u0930\u094d\u0935\u093f\u0915\u0932\u094d\u092a\u093e. Mr. Telang takes it to mean \u2018looking on all things\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":6,\"text\":\"alike.\u2019\",\"end\":\"space\"}],\"uncertain\":true,\"note\":\"The first Sanskrit quotation on line 2 is unclear.\"},\"r7\":{\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"lines\":[{\"n\":1,\"text\":\"Sl. 10. \u092e\u093e\u0928 haughtiness. \u0935\u093f\u0935\u093f\u0915\u094d\u0924\u2014lonely, solitary; p. p. of\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":2,\"text\":\"\u0935\u093f\u091a\u094d with \u0935\u093f. \u092f\u092e\u093f\u0928\u093e\u092e\u094d\u2014of those who restrain their minds ).\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":3,\"text\":\"\",\"end\":\"space\"}],\"uncertain\":true,\"note\":\"The Sanskrit root and punctuation at the end are obscured.\"},\"r1\":{\"type\":\"page_number\",\"lines\":[{\"n\":1,\"text\":\"( 80 )\",\"end\":\"space\"}],\"uncertain\":false,\"note\":null}},\"units\":[{\"id\":\"u1\",\"type\":\"notes\",\"number\":null,\"label\":null,\"open_start\":true,\"open_end\":true,\"children\":[\"u2\",\"u3\",\"u4\",\"u5\",\"u6\",\"u7\"]},{\"id\":\"u2\",\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"number\":\"5\",\"label\":null,\"open_start\":true,\"open_end\":false,\"children\":[\"r2\"]},{\"id\":\"u3\",\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"number\":\"6\",\"label\":null,\"open_start\":false,\"open_end\":false,\"children\":[\"r3\"]},{\"id\":\"u4\",\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"number\":\"7\",\"label\":null,\"open_start\":false,\"open_end\":false,\"children\":[\"r4\"]},{\"id\":\"u5\",\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"number\":\"8\",\"label\":null,\"open_start\":false,\"open_end\":false,\"children\":[\"r5\"]},{\"id\":\"u6\",\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"number\":\"9\",\"label\":null,\"open_start\":false,\"open_end\":false,\"children\":[\"r6\"]},{\"id\":\"u7\",\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"number\":\"10\",\"label\":null,\"open_start\":false,\"open_end\":false,\"children\":[\"r7\"]}],\"flows\":[{\"flow\":\"main\",\"units\":[\"u1\"]}],\"relations\":[]}"
